cat file: Display the contents of a file.

less file: View the contents of a file with pagination.

head file: Display the first few lines of a file.
           By default it will show first 10 lines.
           syntax to see specific number of lines-->  head -n number-of-line file-name--->  head -n 3 file.txt

tail file: Display the last few lines of a file.
            By default it will show last 10 lines
            syntax to see specific number of lines-->  head -n number-of-line file-name--->  tail -n 3 file.txt

grep what-to-search-in-file   file-name: Search for a pattern in a file.
                                        ex: grep if if.py
                    

grep -r what-to-search-in-file   directory-name: Recursively search for a pattern in files within a directory.


